---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageHero from "@dst/ui/PageHero.astro";
---
<Layout
  prose
  title="Family & Lifestyle"
  description="What a Golden Visa actually changes day to day for a family — schooling, healthcare, and settling in — beyond the legal mechanics."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Family & lifestyle"
    title="What changes, day to day"
    image="/covers/family.jpg"
    imageAlt="Cut-paper illustration: four rounded arches of different heights standing side by side."
    imageKind="generated"
  >
    <p class="lede">
      Most of what's written about the Golden Visa stops at eligibility and
      thresholds. What actually matters once you're through that process is
      quieter: a stable base for a family, schools that don't require
      re-applying every year alongside a shorter-term visa, and healthcare
      access that doesn't depend on an employer.
    </p>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Family sponsorship</h2>
    <p>
      A Golden Visa holder can sponsor a spouse and children as dependents,
      with residency terms that track the main visa's long validity rather
      than needing separate short-term renewal. For most families, this is
      the detail that turns "we have residency" into "we've actually
      settled" — one household, one renewal cycle, not several.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Schooling</h2>
    <p>
      Dubai has a large number of international curricula available (British,
      American, IB, and others), and long-term residency removes the
      uncertainty of enrolling a child in a school year you might not still
      be authorised to stay for. Availability at well-regarded schools is
      genuinely competitive — starting the search well before relocating is
      worth doing regardless of visa status.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Healthcare</h2>
    <p>
      Health insurance is mandatory for all UAE residents, Golden Visa
      holders included. Unlike an employment visa, coverage isn't tied to a
      single employer's group policy, which means it doesn't lapse the day a
      job changes — a small detail that matters more than it sounds like it
      should, for anyone who has been through that gap before.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container cta">
    <h2>Next step</h2>
    <p>
      If the property route looks like the right fit, see
      <a href="/properties/" title="Properties that qualify for the Golden Visa">what currently qualifies</a>, or go
      straight to a <a href="/consultation/" title="Request a Golden Visa consultation">consultation</a> to talk through
      your specific situation.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .cta { margin-top: var(--space-5); }
</style>
